   "text": "I read the structure region by region and wrote it as the SMILES below. I did not run it through a parser, so validity is checked by hand only.\n\n**Left side:**\n- A glutarimide (2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl) is attached through its ring nitrogen to an isoindolin-1-one.\n- The isoindolinone carries an alkyne at the 4-position.\n- The alkyne is followed by five CH2 groups and then a C(=O) that acylates a ring nitrogen.\n\n**Central bicycle:**\n- An eight-membered ring contains N(acyl), CH2, CH2, CH (wedged), N, C(=O), CH (wedged, bearing NH) and CH2.\n- The ring is fused through the CH and N to a pyrrolidine.\n- The pyrrolidine CH next to the nitrogen bears a wedged carboxamide.\n\n**Lower left:**\n- The NH on the eight-membered ring is acylated by a benzothiophene-2-carbonyl.\n- The benzothiophene carries a CF2\u2013P(=O)(OH)2 group at C5.\n\n**Right side:**\n- The carboxamide nitrogen is attached to a wedged CH.\n- That CH bears a CH2CH2C(=O)NH2 chain and a thiazole whose 4,5-bond is fused to an indene (the CH2 sits on the sulfur-side carbon).\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I assigned the four wedged stereocentres from the wedge directions and the neighbour positions in the drawing. They are the two ring-fusion and substituent carbons of the bicycle, the carbon bearing the NH, and the side-chain CH.\n\nSMILES: O=C1CCC(C(=O)N1)N2Cc3c(C#CCCCCCC(=O)N4CC[C@H]5CC[C@@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(N)=O)c6nc7c(s6)Cc8ccccc78)N5C(=O)[C@@H](NC(=O)c9cc%10cc(C(F)(F)P(=O)(O)O)ccc%10s9)C4)cccc3C2=O"
